WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.440
(Denis speaking in foreign language)

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:02.273
(bombs exploding)

00:00:02.273 --> 00:00:05.420
(Denis speaking in foreign language)

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:07.570
- [Narrator] At roughly
1:00 PM on March 13th,

00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:09.570
in the Ukrainian city of Mariupol,

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:12.020
resident, Denis Malykhin records video of

00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:14.320
Russian forces striking
apartment buildings

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:16.850
throughout the residential
area around him.

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:19.410
About an hour later, less
than a mile down the street,

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:21.060
another resident, Tymur Rudov,

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:22.820
films the same attack on the neighborhood,

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:24.430
as he and others take cover

00:00:26.087 --> 00:00:28.920
(bombs exploding)

00:00:32.818 --> 00:00:35.485
(Tymur sighing)

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:38.590
Between these two locations,

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:40.150
a photo posted the day before

00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:42.370
shows remnants of what
military experts say

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:43.550
is a cluster bomb,

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:46.700
a weapon that can cause
indiscriminate civilian harm.

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:48.200
They're all fragments of evidence

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:50.640
that have prompted US
officials to accuse Russia of

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:52.200
committing war crimes.

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.280
The Wall Street Journal
verified videos and photos

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:57.110
posted to social media,
analyzed satellite images

00:00:57.110 --> 00:01:00.410
from Maxar Technologies, and
spoke with military strategists

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:01.830
and residents of the city

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:04.150
to reveal a series of
Russian military strikes

00:01:04.150 --> 00:01:06.370
on civilian locations.

00:01:06.370 --> 00:01:08.180
Mariupol is a southern port city

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:12.430
that had a population of
around 450,000 before the war.

00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:14.100
It's strategically important,

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:16.720
linking Russian controlled
parts of Eastern Ukraine

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:19.330
with a swath of territory
the Kremlin has captured

00:01:19.330 --> 00:01:20.580
in the south.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:23.340
The Zhovtnevyi District in
the Western part of the city

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:27.000
is one of the areas most
decimated by Russian attacks.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:29.510
The Journal pieced together
satellite imagery analysis

00:01:29.510 --> 00:01:31.710
from the United Nations and our own data

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:34.480
to show the extent of visible damage.

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:37.640
Footage shot by Tymur Rudov
about a year before the invasion

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:39.594
indicates that this is
a civilian district.

00:01:39.594 --> 00:01:41.030
(soft music)

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:45.470
We can see a shopping
center, apartment complexes,

00:01:45.470 --> 00:01:50.470
a public square, a maternity
hospital, and a theater.

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:55.610
In the four weeks since the
invasion of Mariupol began,

00:01:55.610 --> 00:01:57.963
all of these places have been obliterated.

00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:01.450
Targeting civilians is a playbook

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:05.430
the US government says Russia
used in Chechnya and Syria.

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:08.430
The International Criminal
Court's definition of war crimes

00:02:08.430 --> 00:02:10.860
broadly include willfully killing,

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:14.450
causing suffering, or
deliberately targeting civilians.

00:02:14.450 --> 00:02:16.210
The Russian Embassy in Washington DC

00:02:16.210 --> 00:02:18.100
didn't respond to requests for comment.

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:21.370
The Kremlin has said that it
is not targeting civilians.

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:24.573
Now, we see civilian locations
being attacked in Mariupol.

00:02:25.430 --> 00:02:28.460
Russia has denied using
cluster bombs in Ukraine.

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:30.430
More than a hundred countries
have joined a treaty

00:02:30.430 --> 00:02:31.820
that banned such weapons,

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:34.413
though neither Ukraine
nor Russia is a signatory.

00:02:35.290 --> 00:02:37.950
These types of munitions
release many submunitions,

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:39.840
or small bombs, as they fly,

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:41.750
which can cause widespread civilian harm

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:44.130
in tightly populated areas.

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:47.380
On March 1st, Mariupol's
City Council posted photos of

00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:50.070
missile debris in a
residential neighborhood.

00:02:50.070 --> 00:02:51.680
In other photos of the same debris,

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:54.170
munitions experts said this
Tochka ballistic missile

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:55.240
is a cluster bomb.

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:57.940
The nose cone and tailpiece
of the missile are intact

00:02:57.940 --> 00:02:59.800
and didn't leave large impact craters,

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:01.880
indicating they separated before impact

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:04.850
to release a warhead
containing smaller bombs.

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:06.620
The City Council shared another photo of

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:09.370
a Russian submunition, steps
away from the missile debris,

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:11.560
further evidence that
this was a cluster bomb,

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:13.263
according to munitions experts.

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:16.670
Attacks on civilian locations
in Mariupol began with

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:19.560
Russian forces hitting
civilian infrastructure.

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:22.990
They struck electricity plants
and took out cell towers.

00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:25.500
In early March, we can
see multiple attacks on

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:27.850
Mariupol's food supplies.

00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:29.450
Video posted March third shows

00:03:29.450 --> 00:03:31.780
a smoldering home improvement store.

00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:34.560
Smoke billows from Silpo,
a major grocery store

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:35.543
across the road.

00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:39.090
Satellite imagery days later reveals

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:41.463
the entire shopping center in ruins.

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:43.370
About a mile away,

00:03:43.370 --> 00:03:45.890
videos posted to social
media on March fifth

00:03:45.890 --> 00:03:48.410
show the city's largest mall, Port City,

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:51.000
home to a grocery store,
cafes, and a movie theater,

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:52.033
was also hit.

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:55.320
A satellite image from
around the same time

00:03:55.320 --> 00:03:57.483
shows the entire mall has been flattened.

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:01.363
A video posted later
shows the damage inside.

00:04:06.290 --> 00:04:08.130
After targeting basic infrastructure,

00:04:08.130 --> 00:04:10.770
Russian forces hit houses
and apartment buildings,

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:13.363
leveling large swaths of
residential neighborhoods.

00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:17.370
About halfway between the
two burned shopping centers,

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:18.490
we see a wide view of

00:04:18.490 --> 00:04:21.060
damaged four and eight
story apartment buildings

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:23.113
in a satellite image from March 12th.

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:26.630
In a photo posted to
social media the same day,

00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:28.870
munitions experts say we
can see the remains of

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:32.480
a second banned cluster bomb
in a public square nearby.

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:34.840
Experts say the intact
tail piece indicates

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:36.430
this is the same kind of missile

00:04:36.430 --> 00:04:39.540
confirmed in other cluster
bombings in Ukraine.

00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:42.463
Around it are a pharmacy,
restaurants, and shops.

00:04:45.780 --> 00:04:48.670
The next day, Tymur Rudov
and his neighbors take cover,

00:04:48.670 --> 00:04:51.224
as the apartment buildings
around them are hit.

00:04:51.224 --> 00:04:52.362
(woman speaking in foreign language)

00:04:52.362 --> 00:04:56.294
(man speaking in foreign language)

00:04:56.294 --> 00:04:58.105
(bombs exploding)

00:04:58.105 --> 00:05:00.679
(man speaking in foreign language)

00:05:00.679 --> 00:05:02.603
(bombs exploding)

00:05:02.603 --> 00:05:05.016
(man speaking in foreign language)

00:05:05.016 --> 00:05:07.643
(Tymur sighing)

00:05:07.643 --> 00:05:10.476
(bombs exploding)

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:15.640
Other videos posted to
social media that same week

00:05:15.640 --> 00:05:17.913
show widespread bombing
of homes in the area.

00:05:22.832 --> 00:05:24.968
(bombs exploding)

00:05:24.968 --> 00:05:27.450
(man speaking foreign language)

00:05:27.450 --> 00:05:30.260
On March 19th, Tymur
assesses the destruction of

00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:31.423
a neighbor's apartment.

00:05:34.774 --> 00:05:39.024
(man speaking in foreign language)

00:05:44.059 --> 00:05:46.110
As Russian forces struck residences,

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:49.820
they also began bombing places
like hospitals and shelters,

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:51.720
where residents, including children,

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:53.253
had gone to seek refuge.

00:05:54.090 --> 00:05:56.830
Here, footage shows the aftermath
of the March ninth bombing

00:05:56.830 --> 00:05:58.470
of a maternity hospital,

00:05:58.470 --> 00:06:00.763
which killed three people and injured 17.

00:06:02.890 --> 00:06:04.330
We can see this crater,

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:06.660
which explosives experts
say is indicative of

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:09.823
an airdropped bomb weighing
at least a thousand pounds.

00:06:11.190 --> 00:06:14.150
This woman and her baby died
days after being rescued,

00:06:14.150 --> 00:06:16.610
according to the Associated Press.

00:06:16.610 --> 00:06:19.540
Nearby the hospital,
local, Mikhail Puryshev,

00:06:19.540 --> 00:06:22.550
who regularly evacuates residents
from a bomb shelter there,

00:06:22.550 --> 00:06:24.090
was filming the hospital attack

00:06:24.090 --> 00:06:26.710
when his location came
under fire from the air.

00:06:26.710 --> 00:06:27.668
(man speaking in foreign language)

00:06:27.668 --> 00:06:30.501
(bombs exploding)

00:06:32.242 --> 00:06:35.371
(bombs exploding)

00:06:35.371 --> 00:06:39.621
(man speaking in foreign language)

00:06:40.609 --> 00:06:45.258
(man speaking foreign language)

00:06:45.258 --> 00:06:47.477
(man speaking foreign language)

00:06:47.477 --> 00:06:49.450
(man speaking foreign language)

00:06:49.450 --> 00:06:51.453
Outside, a school across the street,

00:06:53.090 --> 00:06:56.740
and an office building and
cafe behind him are destroyed.

00:06:56.740 --> 00:06:58.430
Less than a mile away from the hospital,

00:06:58.430 --> 00:07:01.660
on March 14th, a satellite
image reveals the word children

00:07:01.660 --> 00:07:04.200
written in Russian on the
ground outside of a theater,

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:07.690
signaling civilians to
anyone flying overhead.

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:10.530
There were more than a
thousand people hiding inside.

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:13.460
The Azov Battalion, a far
right paramilitary group

00:07:13.460 --> 00:07:16.030
that was absorbed into the
Ukrainian National Guard

00:07:16.030 --> 00:07:17.640
posted a video to Telegram

00:07:17.640 --> 00:07:19.970
showing people had taken shelter there.

00:07:19.970 --> 00:07:21.570
Then, on March 16th,

00:07:21.570 --> 00:07:24.070
this video shows the aftermath
of the Russian bombing

00:07:24.070 --> 00:07:25.163
at the same theater.

00:07:28.404 --> 00:07:32.654
(man speaking in foreign language)

00:07:36.490 --> 00:07:39.853
Satellite imagery taken
afterward shows vast destruction.

00:07:40.690 --> 00:07:42.290
Municipal authorities later said

00:07:42.290 --> 00:07:45.403
more than 300 people died in this attack.

00:07:45.403 --> 00:07:46.690
(intense music)

00:07:46.690 --> 00:07:47.970
Local officials estimate

00:07:47.970 --> 00:07:51.250
over 5,000 civilians have been killed.

00:07:51.250 --> 00:07:53.540
On March 28th, the city's mayor called for

00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:56.452
a complete evacuation as
the attacks continued.

00:07:56.452 --> 00:07:59.119
(intense music)

